[32m+[m[32m# Contributing Guide — CyberCba2077[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWelcome to the development workflow of **CyberCba2077**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis document defines the standards and expectations for contributing to the project.[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mThe goal is to ensure code quality, maintainability, and an efficient review process.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll contributors are expected to follow these guidelines.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Development Workflow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe project follows a **feature-driven development workflow** based on GitHub Issues and Pull Requests.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery code change must follow this lifecycle:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. A **task or bug is defined as a GitHub Issue**[m
[32m+[m[32m2. A **developer implements the solution in a branch**[m
[32m+[m[32m3. A **Pull Request (PR) is created**[m
[32m+[m[32m4. The PR is reviewed by:[m
[32m+[m[32m   - a **Tester**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - a **Team Lead**[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Once approved, the PR can be merged.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDirect commits to the main branch are not allowed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Issue Management[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll work must be tracked using GitHub Issues.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach Issue should contain:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- clear description of the problem or feature[m
[32m+[m[32m- acceptance criteria[m
[32m+[m[32m- relevant context[m
[32m+[m[32m- expected behavior[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExample Issue types:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Feature[m
[32m+[m[32m- Bug[m
[32m+[m[32m- Refactor[m
[32m+[m[32m- Documentation[m
[32m+[m[32m- Technical debt[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPull Requests **must reference an Issue**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExample:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCloses #12[m
[32m+[m[32mFixes #8[m
[32m+[m[32mRelated #21[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Branching Strategy[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery change must be implemented in a dedicated branch.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRecommended naming convention:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mfeature/<short-description>[m
[32m+[m[32mbugfix/<short-description>[m
[32m+[m[32mrefactor/<short-description>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExamples:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mfeature/add-inventory-system[m
[32m+[m[32mbugfix/fix-command-parser-crash[m
[32m+[m[32mrefactor/improve-player-ownership[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBranches should remain **focused on a single logical change**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAvoid mixing unrelated modifications.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Pull Request Process[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll changes must be delivered through **Pull Requests**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA Pull Request must:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- reference the related Issue[m
[32m+[m[32m- include a clear description of the change[m
[32m+[m[32m- explain the motivation[m
[32m+[m[32m- provide testing instructions[m
[32m+[m[32m- include evidence when applicable[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA good PR description should answer:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **What changed**[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Why the change was needed**[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **How it was implemented**[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **How reviewers can validate it**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Required PR Checklist[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore requesting a review, the author must ensure:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] The PR references the related Issue[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] The author is assigned to the PR[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] The code compiles successfully[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] The change has a clear and focused purpose[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] The author reviewed their own diff[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] No unrelated changes are included[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Temporary debugging code has been removed[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Naming is clear and consistent[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Documentation is updated if needed[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Tests are updated if applicable[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Code Review Policy[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery Pull Request must be reviewed before merging.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRequired approvals:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Tester approval**[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Team Lead approval**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe review process ensures:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- correctness[m
[32m+[m[32m- maintainability[m
[32m+[m[32m- readability[m
[32m+[m[32m- architectural consistency[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA PR cannot be merged without both approvals.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Tester Responsibilities[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Tester is responsible for validating that:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- the feature behaves as expected[m
[32m+[m[32m- the bug is correctly fixed[m
[32m+[m[32m- the instructions to test the change are reproducible[m
[32m+[m[32m- no regressions are introduced[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Tester must:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- follow the testing instructions in the PR[m
[32m+[m[32m- report issues or unexpected behavior[m
[32m+[m[32m- approve the PR only after validation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Team Lead Responsibilities[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Team Lead is responsible for reviewing:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- architectural consistency[m
[32m+[m[32m- code quality[m
[32m+[m[32m- maintainability[m
[32m+[m[32m- design decisions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Team Lead ensures that:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- the solution aligns with project architecture[m
[32m+[m[32m- code complexity is reasonable[m
[32m+[m[32m- abstractions are appropriate[m
[32m+[m[32m- the change does not introduce technical debt[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# C++ Development Guidelines[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBecause this project is implemented in **C++**, contributors must follow good practices specific to the language.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKey principles:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Prefer RAII[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mResource ownership should be explicit and deterministic.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAvoid manual resource management when possible.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Avoid unnecessary copying[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPrefer:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mconst T&[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mwhen passing large objects.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Respect const-correctness[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFunctions should declare `const` whenever possible.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Use standard containers[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPrefer STL containers (`std::vector`, `std::map`, etc.) over manual memory management.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Keep functions small and focused[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFunctions should ideally perform **one clear responsibility**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Maintain modular design[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mClasses and modules should have well-defined responsibilities.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAvoid tight coupling between components.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Pull Request Size Guidelines[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSmaller PRs are easier to review and safer to merge.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRecommended guideline:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Prefer **small, focused Pull Requests**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Avoid PRs exceeding **~400 lines of changes** when possible[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLarge changes should be split into multiple PRs.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Testing Expectations[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll changes must be validated before merging.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTesting may include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- unit tests[m
[32m+[m[32m- manual validation[m
[32m+[m[32m- scenario testing[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe PR description must include **clear instructions to reproduce and verify the change**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Documentation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCode should be self-explanatory whenever possible.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHowever, documentation must be updated when:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- introducing new systems[m
[32m+[m[32m- changing behavior[m
[32m+[m[32m- modifying public interfaces[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Professional Conduct[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mContributors are expected to behave professionally during the review process.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGuidelines:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- assume good intentions[m
[32m+[m[32m- focus feedback on code, not people[m
[32m+[m[32m- explain reasoning behind suggestions[m
[32m+[m[32m- remain constructive[m
