[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDISABLE_INDEX          = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The GENERATE_TREEVIEW tag is used to specify whether a tree-like index[m
[32m+[m[32m# structure should be generated to display hierarchical information. If the tag[m
[32m+[m[32m# value is set to YES, a side panel will be generated containing a tree-like[m
[32m+[m[32m# index structure (just like the one that is generated for HTML Help). For this[m
[32m+[m[32m# to work a browser that supports JavaScript, DHTML, CSS and frames is required[m
[32m+[m[32m# (i.e. any modern browser). Windows users are probably better off using the[m
[32m+[m[32m# HTML help feature. Via custom style sheets (see HTML_EXTRA_STYLESHEET) one can[m
[32m+[m[32m# further fine tune the look of the index (see "Fine-tuning the output"). As an[m
[32m+[m[32m# example, the default style sheet generated by doxygen has an example that[m
[32m+[m[32m# shows how to put an image at the root of the tree instead of the PROJECT_NAME.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Since the tree basically has the same information as the tab index, you could[m
[32m+[m[32m# consider setting DISABLE_INDEX to YES when enabling this option.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGENERATE_TREEVIEW      = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When both GENERATE_TREEVIEW and DISABLE_INDEX are set to YES, then the[m
[32m+[m[32m# FULL_SIDEBAR option determines if the side bar is limited to only the treeview[m
[32m+[m[32m# area (value NO) or if it should extend to the full height of the window (value[m
[32m+[m[32m# YES). Setting this to YES gives a layout similar to[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://docs.readthedocs.io with more room for contents, but less room for the[m
[32m+[m[32m# project logo, title, and description. If either GENERATE_TREEVIEW or[m
[32m+[m[32m# DISABLE_INDEX is set to NO, this option has no effect.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFULL_SIDEBAR           = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The ENUM_VALUES_PER_LINE tag can be used to set the number of enum values that[m
[32m+[m[32m# doxygen will group on one line in the generated HTML documentation.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note that a value of 0 will completely suppress the enum values from appearing[m
[32m+[m[32m# in the overview section.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 20, default value: 4.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mENUM_VALUES_PER_LINE   = 4[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the treeview is enabled (see GENERATE_TREEVIEW) then this tag can be used[m
[32m+[m[32m# to set the initial width (in pixels) of the frame in which the tree is shown.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 1500, default value: 250.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTREEVIEW_WIDTH         = 250[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the EXT_LINKS_IN_WINDOW option is set to YES, doxygen will open links to[m
[32m+[m[32m# external symbols imported via tag files in a separate window.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXT_LINKS_IN_WINDOW    = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the OBFUSCATE_EMAILS tag is set to YES, doxygen will obfuscate email[m
[32m+[m[32m# addresses.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOBFUSCATE_EMAILS       = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the HTML_FORMULA_FORMAT option is set to svg, doxygen will use the pdf2svg[m
[32m+[m[32m# tool (see https://github.com/dawbarton/pdf2svg) or inkscape (see[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://inkscape.org) to generate formulas as SVG images instead of PNGs for[m
[32m+[m[32m# the HTML output. These images will generally look nicer at scaled resolutions.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: png (the default) and svg (looks nicer but requires the[m
[32m+[m[32m# pdf2svg or inkscape tool).[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: png.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHTML_FORMULA_FORMAT    = png[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Use this tag to change the font size of LaTeX formulas included as images in[m
[32m+[m[32m# the HTML documentation. When you change the font size after a successful[m
[32m+[m[32m# doxygen run you need to manually remove any form_*.png images from the HTML[m
[32m+[m[32m# output directory to force them to be regenerated.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 8, maximum value: 50, default value: 10.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFORMULA_FONTSIZE       = 10[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The FORMULA_MACROFILE can contain LaTeX \newcommand and \renewcommand commands[m
[32m+[m[32m# to create new LaTeX commands to be used in formulas as building blocks. See[m
[32m+[m[32m# the section "Including formulas" for details.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFORMULA_MACROFILE      =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# Enable the USE_MATHJAX option to render LaTeX formulas using MathJax (see[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://www.mathjax.org) which uses client side JavaScript for the rendering[m
[32m+[m[32m# instead of using pre-rendered bitmaps. Use this if you do not have LaTeX[m
[32m+[m[32m# installed or if you want to formulas look prettier in the HTML output. When[m
[32m+[m[32m# enabled you may also need to install MathJax separately and configure the path[m
[32m+[m[32m# to it using the MATHJAX_RELPATH option.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUSE_MATHJAX            = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# With MATHJAX_VERSION it is possible to specify the MathJax version to be used.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note that the different versions of MathJax have different requirements with[m
[32m+[m[32m# regards to the different settings, so it is possible that also other MathJax[m
[32m+[m[32m# settings have to be changed when switching between the different MathJax[m
[32m+[m[32m# versions.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: MathJax_2 and MathJax_3.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: MathJax_2.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag USE_MATHJAX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMATHJAX_VERSION        = MathJax_2[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When MathJax is enabled you can set the default output format to be used for[m
[32m+[m[32m# the MathJax output. For more details about the output format see MathJax[m
[32m+[m[32m# version 2 (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# http://docs.mathjax.org/en/v2.7-latest/output.html) and MathJax version 3[m
[32m+[m[32m# (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# http://docs.mathjax.org/en/latest/web/components/output.html).[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: HTML-CSS (which is slower, but has the best[m
[32m+[m[32m# compatibility. This is the name for Mathjax version 2, for MathJax version 3[m
[32m+[m[32m# this will be translated into chtml), NativeMML (i.e. MathML. Only supported[m
[32m+[m[32m# for NathJax 2. For MathJax version 3 chtml will be used instead.), chtml (This[m
[32m+[m[32m# is the name for Mathjax version 3, for MathJax version 2 this will be[m
[32m+[m[32m# translated into HTML-CSS) and SVG.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: HTML-CSS.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag USE_MATHJAX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMATHJAX_FORMAT         = HTML-CSS[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When MathJax is enabled you need to specify the location relative to the HTML[m
[32m+[m[32m# output directory using the MATHJAX_RELPATH option. The destination directory[m
[32m+[m[32m# should contain the MathJax.js script. For instance, if the mathjax directory[m
[32m+[m[32m# is located at the same level as the HTML output directory, then[m
[32m+[m[32m# MATHJAX_RELPATH should be ../mathjax. The default value points to the MathJax[m
[32m+[m[32m# Content Delivery Network so you can quickly see the result without installing[m
[32m+[m[32m# MathJax. However, it is strongly recommended to install a local copy of[m
[32m+[m[32m# MathJax from https://www.mathjax.org before deployment. The default value is:[m
[32m+[m[32m# - in case of MathJax version 2: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@2[m
[32m+[m[32m# - in case of MathJax version 3: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag USE_MATHJAX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMATHJAX_RELPATH        =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The MATHJAX_EXTENSIONS tag can be used to specify one or more MathJax[m
[32m+[m[32m# extension names that should be enabled during MathJax rendering. For example[m
[32m+[m[32m# for MathJax version 2 (see[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://docs.mathjax.org/en/v2.7-latest/tex.html#tex-and-latex-extensions):[m
[32m+[m[32m# MATHJAX_EXTENSIONS = TeX/AMSmath TeX/AMSsymbols[m
[32m+[m[32m# For example for MathJax version 3 (see[m
[32m+[m[32m# http://docs.mathjax.org/en/latest/input/tex/extensions/index.html):[m
[32m+[m[32m# MATHJAX_EXTENSIONS = ams[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag USE_MATHJAX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMATHJAX_EXTENSIONS     =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The MATHJAX_CODEFILE tag can be used to specify a file with javascript pieces[m
[32m+[m[32m# of code that will be used on startup of the MathJax code. See the MathJax site[m
[32m+[m[32m# (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# http://docs.mathjax.org/en/v2.7-latest/output.html) for more details. For an[m
[32m+[m[32m# example see the documentation.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag USE_MATHJAX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMATHJAX_CODEFILE       =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When the SEARCHENGINE tag is enabled doxygen will generate a search box for[m
[32m+[m[32m# the HTML output. The underlying search engine uses javascript and DHTML and[m
[32m+[m[32m# should work on any modern browser. Note that when using HTML help[m
[32m+[m[32m# (GENERATE_HTMLHELP), Qt help (GENERATE_QHP), or docsets (GENERATE_DOCSET)[m
[32m+[m[32m# there is already a search function so this one should typically be disabled.[m
[32m+[m[32m# For large projects the javascript based search engine can be slow, then[m
[32m+[m[32m# enabling SERVER_BASED_SEARCH may provide a better solution. It is possible to[m
[32m+[m[32m# search using the keyboard; to jump to the search box use <access key> + S[m
[32m+[m[32m# (what the <access key> is depends on the OS and browser, but it is typically[m
[32m+[m[32m# <CTRL>, <ALT>/<option>, or both). Inside the search box use the <cursor down[m
[32m+[m[32m# key> to jump into the search results window, the results can be navigated[m
[32m+[m[32m# using the <cursor keys>. Press <Enter> to select an item or <escape> to cancel[m
[32m+[m[32m# the search. The filter options can be selected when the cursor is inside the[m
[32m+[m[32m# search box by pressing <Shift>+<cursor down>. Also here use the <cursor keys>[m
[32m+[m[32m# to select a filter and <Enter> or <escape> to activate or cancel the filter[m
[32m+[m[32m# option.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_HTML is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSEARCHENGINE           = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When the SERVER_BASED_SEARCH tag is enabled the search engine will be[m
[32m+[m[32m# implemented using a web server instead of a web client using JavaScript. There[m
[32m+[m[32m# are two flavors of web server based searching depending on the EXTERNAL_SEARCH[m
[32m+[m[32m# setting. When disabled, doxygen will generate a PHP script for searching and[m
[32m+[m[32m# an index file used by the script. When EXTERNAL_SEARCH is enabled the indexing[m
[32m+[m[32m# and searching needs to be provided by external tools. See the section[m
[32m+[m[32m# "External Indexing and Searching" for details.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag SEARCHENGINE is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSERVER_BASED_SEARCH    = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When EXTERNAL_SEARCH tag is enabled doxygen will no longer generate the PHP[m
[32m+[m[32m# script for searching. Instead the search results are written to an XML file[m
[32m+[m[32m# which needs to be processed by an external indexer. Doxygen will invoke an[m
[32m+[m[32m# external search engine pointed to by the SEARCHENGINE_URL option to obtain the[m
[32m+[m[32m# search results.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Doxygen ships with an example indexer (doxyindexer) and search engine[m
[32m+[m[32m# (doxysearch.cgi) which are based on the open source search engine library[m
[32m+[m[32m# Xapian (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://xapian.org/).[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# See the section "External Indexing and Searching" for details.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag SEARCHENGINE is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXTERNAL_SEARCH        = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The SEARCHENGINE_URL should point to a search engine hosted by a web server[m
[32m+[m[32m# which will return the search results when EXTERNAL_SEARCH is enabled.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Doxygen ships with an example indexer (doxyindexer) and search engine[m
[32m+[m[32m# (doxysearch.cgi) which are based on the open source search engine library[m
[32m+[m[32m# Xapian (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://xapian.org/). See the section "External Indexing and Searching" for[m
[32m+[m[32m# details.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag SEARCHENGINE is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSEARCHENGINE_URL       =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When SERVER_BASED_SEARCH and EXTERNAL_SEARCH are both enabled the unindexed[m
[32m+[m[32m# search data is written to a file for indexing by an external tool. With the[m
[32m+[m[32m# SEARCHDATA_FILE tag the name of this file can be specified.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default file is: searchdata.xml.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag SEARCHENGINE is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSEARCHDATA_FILE        = searchdata.xml[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When SERVER_BASED_SEARCH and EXTERNAL_SEARCH are both enabled the[m
[32m+[m[32m# EXTERNAL_SEARCH_ID tag can be used as an identifier for the project. This is[m
[32m+[m[32m# useful in combination with EXTRA_SEARCH_MAPPINGS to search through multiple[m
[32m+[m[32m# projects and redirect the results back to the right project.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag SEARCHENGINE is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXTERNAL_SEARCH_ID     =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The EXTRA_SEARCH_MAPPINGS tag can be used to enable searching through doxygen[m
[32m+[m[32m# projects other than the one defined by this configuration file, but that are[m
[32m+[m[32m# all added to the same external search index. Each project needs to have a[m
[32m+[m[32m# unique id set via EXTERNAL_SEARCH_ID. The search mapping then maps the id of[m
[32m+[m[32m# to a relative location where the documentation can be found. The format is:[m
[32m+[m[32m# EXTRA_SEARCH_MAPPINGS = tagname1=loc1 tagname2=loc2 ...[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag SEARCHENGINE is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXTRA_SEARCH_MAPPINGS  =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32m# Configuration options related to the LaTeX output[m
[32m+[m[32m#---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the GENERATE_LATEX tag is set to YES, doxygen will generate LaTeX output.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGENERATE_LATEX         = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The LATEX_OUTPUT tag is used to specify where the LaTeX docs will be put. If a[m
[32m+[m[32m# relative path is entered the value of OUTPUT_DIRECTORY will be put in front of[m
[32m+[m[32m# it.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default directory is: latex.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLATEX_OUTPUT           = latex[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The LATEX_CMD_NAME tag can be used to specify the LaTeX command name to be[m
[32m+[m[32m# invoked.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note that when not enabling USE_PDFLATEX the default is latex when enabling[m
[32m+[m[32m# USE_PDFLATEX the default is pdflatex and when in the later case latex is[m
[32m+[m[32m# chosen this is overwritten by pdflatex. For specific output languages the[m
[32m+[m[32m# default can have been set differently, this depends on the implementation of[m
[32m+[m[32m# the output language.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLATEX_CMD_NAME         =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The MAKEINDEX_CMD_NAME tag can be used to specify the command name to generate[m
[32m+[m[32m# index for LaTeX.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note: This tag is used in the Makefile / make.bat.[m
[32m+[m[32m# See also: LATEX_MAKEINDEX_CMD for the part in the generated output file[m
[32m+[m[32m# (.tex).[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default file is: makeindex.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMAKEINDEX_CMD_NAME     = makeindex[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The LATEX_MAKEINDEX_CMD tag can be used to specify the command name to[m
[32m+[m[32m# generate index for LaTeX. In case there is no backslash (\) as first character[m
[32m+[m[32m# it will be automatically added in the LaTeX code.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note: This tag is used in the generated output file (.tex).[m
[32m+[m[32m# See also: MAKEINDEX_CMD_NAME for the part in the Makefile / make.bat.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: makeindex.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLATEX_MAKEINDEX_CMD    = makeindex[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the COMPACT_LATEX tag is set to YES, doxygen generates more compact LaTeX[m
[32m+[m[32m# documents. This may be useful for small projects and may help to save some[m
[32m+[m[32m# trees in general.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCOMPACT_LATEX          = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The PAPER_TYPE tag can be used to set the paper type that is used by the[m
[32m+[m[32m# printer.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: a4 (210 x 297 mm), letter (8.5 x 11 inches), legal (8.5 x[m
[32m+[m[32m# 14 inches) and executive (7.25 x 10.5 inches).[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: a4.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPAPER_TYPE             = a4[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The EXTRA_PACKAGES tag can be used to specify one or more LaTeX package names[m
[32m+[m[32m# that should be included in the LaTeX output. The package can be specified just[m
[32m+[m[32m# by its name or with the correct syntax as to be used with the LaTeX[m
[32m+[m[32m# \usepackage command. To get the times font for instance you can specify :[m
[32m+[m[32m# EXTRA_PACKAGES=times or EXTRA_PACKAGES={times}[m
[32m+[m[32m# To use the option intlimits with the amsmath package you can specify:[m
[32m+[m[32m# EXTRA_PACKAGES=[intlimits]{amsmath}[m
[32m+[m[32m# If left blank no extra packages will be included.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag GENERATE_LATEX is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXTRA_PACKAGES         =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The LATEX_HEADER tag can be used to specify a user-defined LaTeX header for[m
[32m+[m[32m# the generated LaTeX document. The header should contain everything until the[m
[32m+[m[32m# first chapter. If it is left blank doxygen will generate a standard header. It[m
[32m+[m[32m# is highly recommended to start with a default header using[m
[32m+[m[32m# doxygen -w latex new_header.tex new_footer.tex new_stylesheet.sty[m
[32m+[m[32m# and then modify the file new_header.tex. See also section "Doxygen usage" for[m
[32m+[m[32m# information on how to generate the default header that doxygen normally uses.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
