[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag ENABLE_PREPROCESSING is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mINCLUDE_FILE_PATTERNS  =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The PREDEFINED tag can be used to specify one or more macro names that are[m
[32m+[m[32m# defined before the preprocessor is started (similar to the -D option of e.g.[m
[32m+[m[32m# gcc). The argument of the tag is a list of macros of the form: name or[m
[32m+[m[32m# name=definition (no spaces). If the definition and the "=" are omitted, "=1"[m
[32m+[m[32m# is assumed. To prevent a macro definition from being undefined via #undef or[m
[32m+[m[32m# recursively expanded use the := operator instead of the = operator.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag ENABLE_PREPROCESSING is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPREDEFINED             =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the MACRO_EXPANSION and EXPAND_ONLY_PREDEF tags are set to YES then this[m
[32m+[m[32m# tag can be used to specify a list of macro names that should be expanded. The[m
[32m+[m[32m# macro definition that is found in the sources will be used. Use the PREDEFINED[m
[32m+[m[32m# tag if you want to use a different macro definition that overrules the[m
[32m+[m[32m# definition found in the source code.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag ENABLE_PREPROCESSING is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXPAND_AS_DEFINED      =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the SKIP_FUNCTION_MACROS tag is set to YES then doxygen's preprocessor will[m
[32m+[m[32m# remove all references to function-like macros that are alone on a line, have[m
[32m+[m[32m# an all uppercase name, and do not end with a semicolon. Such function macros[m
[32m+[m[32m# are typically used for boiler-plate code, and will confuse the parser if not[m
[32m+[m[32m# removed.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag ENABLE_PREPROCESSING is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSKIP_FUNCTION_MACROS   = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32m# Configuration options related to external references[m
[32m+[m[32m#---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The TAGFILES tag can be used to specify one or more tag files. For each tag[m
[32m+[m[32m# file the location of the external documentation should be added. The format of[m
[32m+[m[32m# a tag file without this location is as follows:[m
[32m+[m[32m# TAGFILES = file1 file2 ...[m
[32m+[m[32m# Adding location for the tag files is done as follows:[m
[32m+[m[32m# TAGFILES = file1=loc1 "file2 = loc2" ...[m
[32m+[m[32m# where loc1 and loc2 can be relative or absolute paths or URLs. See the[m
[32m+[m[32m# section "Linking to external documentation" for more information about the use[m
[32m+[m[32m# of tag files.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note: Each tag file must have a unique name (where the name does NOT include[m
[32m+[m[32m# the path). If a tag file is not located in the directory in which doxygen is[m
[32m+[m[32m# run, you must also specify the path to the tagfile here.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTAGFILES               =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# When a file name is specified after GENERATE_TAGFILE, doxygen will create a[m
[32m+[m[32m# tag file that is based on the input files it reads. See section "Linking to[m
[32m+[m[32m# external documentation" for more information about the usage of tag files.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGENERATE_TAGFILE       =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the ALLEXTERNALS tag is set to YES, all external classes and namespaces[m
[32m+[m[32m# will be listed in the class and namespace index. If set to NO, only the[m
[32m+[m[32m# inherited external classes will be listed.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mALLEXTERNALS           = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the EXTERNAL_GROUPS tag is set to YES, all external groups will be listed[m
[32m+[m[32m# in the topic index. If set to NO, only the current project's groups will be[m
[32m+[m[32m# listed.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXTERNAL_GROUPS        = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the EXTERNAL_PAGES tag is set to YES, all external pages will be listed in[m
[32m+[m[32m# the related pages index. If set to NO, only the current project's pages will[m
[32m+[m[32m# be listed.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEXTERNAL_PAGES         = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32m# Configuration options related to diagram generator tools[m
[32m+[m[32m#---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If set to YES the inheritance and collaboration graphs will hide inheritance[m
[32m+[m[32m# and usage relations if the target is undocumented or is not a class.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHIDE_UNDOC_RELATIONS   = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If you set the HAVE_DOT tag to YES then doxygen will assume the dot tool is[m
[32m+[m[32m# available from the path. This tool is part of Graphviz (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://www.graphviz.org/), a graph visualization toolkit from AT&T and Lucent[m
[32m+[m[32m# Bell Labs. The other options in this section have no effect if this option is[m
[32m+[m[32m# set to NO[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHAVE_DOT               = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The DOT_NUM_THREADS specifies the number of dot invocations doxygen is allowed[m
[32m+[m[32m# to run in parallel. When set to 0 doxygen will base this on the number of[m
[32m+[m[32m# processors available in the system. You can set it explicitly to a value[m
[32m+[m[32m# larger than 0 to get control over the balance between CPU load and processing[m
[32m+[m[32m# speed.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 32, default value: 0.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_NUM_THREADS        = 0[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# DOT_COMMON_ATTR is common attributes for nodes, edges and labels of[m
[32m+[m[32m# subgraphs. When you want a differently looking font in the dot files that[m
[32m+[m[32m# doxygen generates you can specify fontname, fontcolor and fontsize attributes.[m
[32m+[m[32m# For details please see <a href=https://graphviz.org/doc/info/attrs.html>Node,[m
[32m+[m[32m# Edge and Graph Attributes specification</a> You need to make sure dot is able[m
[32m+[m[32m# to find the font, which can be done by putting it in a standard location or by[m
[32m+[m[32m# setting the DOTFONTPATH environment variable or by setting DOT_FONTPATH to the[m
[32m+[m[32m# directory containing the font. Default graphviz fontsize is 14.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: fontname=Helvetica,fontsize=10.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_COMMON_ATTR        = "fontname=Helvetica,fontsize=10"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# DOT_EDGE_ATTR is concatenated with DOT_COMMON_ATTR. For elegant style you can[m
[32m+[m[32m# add 'arrowhead=open, arrowtail=open, arrowsize=0.5'. <a[m
[32m+[m[32m# href=https://graphviz.org/doc/info/arrows.html>Complete documentation about[m
[32m+[m[32m# arrows shapes.</a>[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: labelfontname=Helvetica,labelfontsize=10.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_EDGE_ATTR          = "labelfontname=Helvetica,labelfontsize=10"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# DOT_NODE_ATTR is concatenated with DOT_COMMON_ATTR. For view without boxes[m
[32m+[m[32m# around nodes set 'shape=plain' or 'shape=plaintext' <a[m
[32m+[m[32m# href=https://www.graphviz.org/doc/info/shapes.html>Shapes specification</a>[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: shape=box,height=0.2,width=0.4.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_NODE_ATTR          = "shape=box,height=0.2,width=0.4"[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# You can set the path where dot can find font specified with fontname in[m
[32m+[m[32m# DOT_COMMON_ATTR and others dot attributes.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_FONTPATH           =[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the CLASS_GRAPH tag is set to YES or GRAPH or BUILTIN then doxygen will[m
[32m+[m[32m# generate a graph for each documented class showing the direct and indirect[m
[32m+[m[32m# inheritance relations. In case the CLASS_GRAPH tag is set to YES or GRAPH and[m
[32m+[m[32m# HAVE_DOT is enabled as well, then dot will be used to draw the graph. In case[m
[32m+[m[32m# the CLASS_GRAPH tag is set to YES and HAVE_DOT is disabled or if the[m
[32m+[m[32m# CLASS_GRAPH tag is set to BUILTIN, then the built-in generator will be used.[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the CLASS_GRAPH tag is set to TEXT the direct and indirect inheritance[m
[32m+[m[32m# relations will be shown as texts / links. Explicit enabling an inheritance[m
[32m+[m[32m# graph or choosing a different representation for an inheritance graph of a[m
[32m+[m[32m# specific class, can be accomplished by means of the command \inheritancegraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Disabling an inheritance graph can be accomplished by means of the command[m
[32m+[m[32m# \hideinheritancegraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: NO, YES, TEXT, GRAPH and BUILTIN.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCLASS_GRAPH            = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the COLLABORATION_GRAPH tag is set to YES then doxygen will generate a[m
[32m+[m[32m# graph for each documented class showing the direct and indirect implementation[m
[32m+[m[32m# dependencies (inheritance, containment, and class references variables) of the[m
[32m+[m[32m# class with other documented classes. Explicit enabling a collaboration graph,[m
[32m+[m[32m# when COLLABORATION_GRAPH is set to NO, can be accomplished by means of the[m
[32m+[m[32m# command \collaborationgraph. Disabling a collaboration graph can be[m
[32m+[m[32m# accomplished by means of the command \hidecollaborationgraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCOLLABORATION_GRAPH    = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the GROUP_GRAPHS tag is set to YES then doxygen will generate a graph for[m
[32m+[m[32m# groups, showing the direct groups dependencies. Explicit enabling a group[m
[32m+[m[32m# dependency graph, when GROUP_GRAPHS is set to NO, can be accomplished by means[m
[32m+[m[32m# of the command \groupgraph. Disabling a directory graph can be accomplished by[m
[32m+[m[32m# means of the command \hidegroupgraph. See also the chapter Grouping in the[m
[32m+[m[32m# manual.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGROUP_GRAPHS           = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the UML_LOOK tag is set to YES, doxygen will generate inheritance and[m
[32m+[m[32m# collaboration diagrams in a style similar to the OMG's Unified Modeling[m
[32m+[m[32m# Language.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUML_LOOK               = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the UML_LOOK tag is enabled, the fields and methods are shown inside the[m
[32m+[m[32m# class node. If there are many fields or methods and many nodes the graph may[m
[32m+[m[32m# become too big to be useful. The UML_LIMIT_NUM_FIELDS threshold limits the[m
[32m+[m[32m# number of items for each type to make the size more manageable. Set this to 0[m
[32m+[m[32m# for no limit. Note that the threshold may be exceeded by 50% before the limit[m
[32m+[m[32m# is enforced. So when you set the threshold to 10, up to 15 fields may appear,[m
[32m+[m[32m# but if the number exceeds 15, the total amount of fields shown is limited to[m
[32m+[m[32m# 10.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 100, default value: 10.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag UML_LOOK is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUML_LIMIT_NUM_FIELDS   = 10[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the DOT_UML_DETAILS tag is set to NO, doxygen will show attributes and[m
[32m+[m[32m# methods without types and arguments in the UML graphs. If the DOT_UML_DETAILS[m
[32m+[m[32m# tag is set to YES, doxygen will add type and arguments for attributes and[m
[32m+[m[32m# methods in the UML graphs. If the DOT_UML_DETAILS tag is set to NONE, doxygen[m
[32m+[m[32m# will not generate fields with class member information in the UML graphs. The[m
[32m+[m[32m# class diagrams will look similar to the default class diagrams but using UML[m
[32m+[m[32m# notation for the relationships.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: NO, YES and NONE.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag UML_LOOK is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_UML_DETAILS        = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The DOT_WRAP_THRESHOLD tag can be used to set the maximum number of characters[m
[32m+[m[32m# to display on a single line. If the actual line length exceeds this threshold[m
[32m+[m[32m# significantly it will be wrapped across multiple lines. Some heuristics are[m
[32m+[m[32m# applied to avoid ugly line breaks.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 0, maximum value: 1000, default value: 17.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_WRAP_THRESHOLD     = 17[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the TEMPLATE_RELATIONS tag is set to YES then the inheritance and[m
[32m+[m[32m# collaboration graphs will show the relations between templates and their[m
[32m+[m[32m# instances.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTEMPLATE_RELATIONS     = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the INCLUDE_GRAPH, ENABLE_PREPROCESSING and SEARCH_INCLUDES tags are set to[m
[32m+[m[32m# YES then doxygen will generate a graph for each documented file showing the[m
[32m+[m[32m# direct and indirect include dependencies of the file with other documented[m
[32m+[m[32m# files. Explicit enabling an include graph, when INCLUDE_GRAPH is is set to NO,[m
[32m+[m[32m# can be accomplished by means of the command \includegraph. Disabling an[m
[32m+[m[32m# include graph can be accomplished by means of the command \hideincludegraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mINCLUDE_GRAPH          = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the INCLUDED_BY_GRAPH, ENABLE_PREPROCESSING and SEARCH_INCLUDES tags are[m
[32m+[m[32m# set to YES then doxygen will generate a graph for each documented file showing[m
[32m+[m[32m# the direct and indirect include dependencies of the file with other documented[m
[32m+[m[32m# files. Explicit enabling an included by graph, when INCLUDED_BY_GRAPH is set[m
[32m+[m[32m# to NO, can be accomplished by means of the command \includedbygraph. Disabling[m
[32m+[m[32m# an included by graph can be accomplished by means of the command[m
[32m+[m[32m# \hideincludedbygraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mINCLUDED_BY_GRAPH      = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the CALL_GRAPH tag is set to YES then doxygen will generate a call[m
[32m+[m[32m# dependency graph for every global function or class method.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note that enabling this option will significantly increase the time of a run.[m
[32m+[m[32m# So in most cases it will be better to enable call graphs for selected[m
[32m+[m[32m# functions only using the \callgraph command. Disabling a call graph can be[m
[32m+[m[32m# accomplished by means of the command \hidecallgraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCALL_GRAPH             = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the CALLER_GRAPH tag is set to YES then doxygen will generate a caller[m
[32m+[m[32m# dependency graph for every global function or class method.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note that enabling this option will significantly increase the time of a run.[m
[32m+[m[32m# So in most cases it will be better to enable caller graphs for selected[m
[32m+[m[32m# functions only using the \callergraph command. Disabling a caller graph can be[m
[32m+[m[32m# accomplished by means of the command \hidecallergraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCALLER_GRAPH           = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the GRAPHICAL_HIERARCHY tag is set to YES then doxygen will graphical[m
[32m+[m[32m# hierarchy of all classes instead of a textual one.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mGRAPHICAL_HIERARCHY    = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If the DIRECTORY_GRAPH tag is set to YES then doxygen will show the[m
[32m+[m[32m# dependencies a directory has on other directories in a graphical way. The[m
[32m+[m[32m# dependency relations are determined by the #include relations between the[m
[32m+[m[32m# files in the directories. Explicit enabling a directory graph, when[m
[32m+[m[32m# DIRECTORY_GRAPH is set to NO, can be accomplished by means of the command[m
[32m+[m[32m# \directorygraph. Disabling a directory graph can be accomplished by means of[m
[32m+[m[32m# the command \hidedirectorygraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: YES.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDIRECTORY_GRAPH        = YES[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The DIR_GRAPH_MAX_DEPTH tag can be used to limit the maximum number of levels[m
[32m+[m[32m# of child directories generated in directory dependency graphs by dot.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Minimum value: 1, maximum value: 25, default value: 1.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag DIRECTORY_GRAPH is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDIR_GRAPH_MAX_DEPTH    = 1[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The DOT_IMAGE_FORMAT tag can be used to set the image format of the images[m
[32m+[m[32m# generated by dot. For an explanation of the image formats see the section[m
[32m+[m[32m# output formats in the documentation of the dot tool (Graphviz (see:[m
[32m+[m[32m# https://www.graphviz.org/)).[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note: If you choose svg you need to set HTML_FILE_EXTENSION to xhtml in order[m
[32m+[m[32m# to make the SVG files visible in IE 9+ (other browsers do not have this[m
[32m+[m[32m# requirement).[m
[32m+[m[32m# Possible values are: png, jpg, gif, svg, png:gd, png:gd:gd, png:cairo,[m
[32m+[m[32m# png:cairo:gd, png:cairo:cairo, png:cairo:gdiplus, png:gdiplus and[m
[32m+[m[32m# png:gdiplus:gdiplus.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: png.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_IMAGE_FORMAT       = png[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# If DOT_IMAGE_FORMAT is set to svg, then this option can be set to YES to[m
[32m+[m[32m# enable generation of interactive SVG images that allow zooming and panning.[m
[32m+[m[32m#[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note that this requires a modern browser other than Internet Explorer. Tested[m
[32m+[m[32m# and working are Firefox, Chrome, Safari, and Opera.[m
[32m+[m[32m# Note: For IE 9+ you need to set HTML_FILE_EXTENSION to xhtml in order to make[m
[32m+[m[32m# the SVG files visible. Older versions of IE do not have SVG support.[m
[32m+[m[32m# The default value is: NO.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mINTERACTIVE_SVG        = NO[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m# The DOT_PATH tag can be used to specify the path where the dot tool can be[m
[32m+[m[32m# found. If left blank, it is assumed the dot tool can be found in the path.[m
[32m+[m[32m# This tag requires that the tag HAVE_DOT is set to YES.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDOT_PATH               =[m
[32m+[m
